  <String key="Mod.Description">3D clouds, shadows, rain, fog</String>
  <String key="Mod.Unsupported">
    Volumetric Weather could not draw its clouds on this computer, so it has switched itself
    off: nothing in this city is changed by it.\n\n
    The mod needs Metal or OpenGL 3.3, and the game does not have either here. If the game is
    started with a launch option that changes its graphics (Steam: right-click the game,
    Properties, Launch Options), remove it and restart the game.
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.UnsupportedLinux">
    Volumetric Weather could not draw its clouds on this computer, so it has switched itself
    off: nothing in this city is changed by it.\n\n
    The mod needs OpenGL 3.3, and the game does not have it here. If the game is started with a
    launch option that changes its graphics (Steam: right-click the game, Properties, Launch
    Options), remove it and restart the game.\n\n
    The Windows version of the game runs the mod through Proton: Steam, right-click the game,
    Properties, Compatibility, check "Force the use of a specific Steam Play compatibility tool"
    and pick a Proton version.
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.UnsupportedWindows">
    Volumetric Weather could not draw its clouds on this PC, so it has switched itself off:
    nothing in this city is changed by it.\n\n
    The usual causes:\n
    - the game is started with a launch option such as -force-d3d9, or -force-glcore on a
    graphics card whose OpenGL is older than 3.3 (Steam: right-click the game, Properties,
    Launch Options). Remove it, and restart the game.\n
    - the graphics card is older than DirectX 10.\n\n
    If neither applies, please report it in the comments on the mod's Workshop page, with this
    file:\n
    {0}
  </String>
  <String key="Mod.ExperimentalPlatformNote">
    Mac and Linux support is new and experimental. If the game stutters, pick the Low quality preset.
  </String>

